                <pb facs="0770" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/190: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-20T22:00:00+08:00">November 20, 1929—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 21—2:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1018. Local press today carries article, pertinent portions of which follow:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Determination to effect the abolition of extraterritoriality on January
                            1st next was reaffirmed by Dr. C. T. Wang, Monday<anchor n="24"
                                xml:id="d635-f1"/> morning, according to Chinese telegraphic advices
                            from Nanking. Touching on the subject of extraterritoriality, the
                            Foreign Minister said that China was the only country in the world where
                            this archaic system prevailed, and that the Chinese report says that the
                            Nanking Government has decided not recognize the rendition agreement
                            which was negotiated by Dr. V. C. [<hi rendition="#italic">K</hi>.] Ting
                            and the foreign consuls in Shanghai in 1926<anchor n="25"
                                xml:id="d635-f2"/> when General Sun Chuan-fang was at the head of
                            the Kiangsu provincial government.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
